{"title":"2009 IMO Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_IMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Determine all functions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> from the set of positive integers to the set of positive integers such that, for all positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, there exists a non-degenerate triangle with sides of lengths \n</p>\n<center> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/6/8e645a0393a2bb5633d525e276321203781753af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,f(b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"49\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/2/7e24db20845eba2e50f55b74a222d4ef4858c53a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(b+f(a)-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"119\" height=\"18\" />. </center>\n<p>(A triangle is <i>non-degenerate</i> if its vertices are not collinear.) \n</p><p><i>Author: Bruno Le Floch, France</i>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_IMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Answer: The only such function is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/7/4874544e2638f3712dbb70e5ccf37558a5fc0acb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)=x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"69\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>It is easy to see that this function satisfy the condition. We are going to proof that this is the only such function. \n</p><p>We start with\n</p><p>Lemma. If 1, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> are sides of a non-degenerate triangle then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/b/5abd2c942ae299fd26e18d0ca5d390a7ca4a8c34.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=b$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p>Proof. In this case <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/c/46c601bb05dde2137874d60f6e667882905e92d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&lt;b+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"72\" height=\"14\" />, therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/e/35e1900f9ae83cebcbb5735f6c7bd6b6c505ba55.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a \\le b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" />. By the same reason, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/b/23bf419c2c1fdcaeb436dd3913905a99d62a6330.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b \\le a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"17\" />. Therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/b/5abd2c942ae299fd26e18d0ca5d390a7ca4a8c34.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=b$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/9/5b94e6c20e58291aec1f2d4faada4bdf12705a4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u=f(1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"67\" height=\"18\" />. Now consider the given condition for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/2/502e059d1a020b368aee3a99c5669d88331d321f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />. By Lemma we get that \n</p>\n<center> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/0/4805b0a000399510ffe1dcbafe0605026493f1e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(b)=f(b+u-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"152\" height=\"18\" /> for any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />.  </center>\n<p>First, suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/9/e19980c021a567022376a78a87f6094c8aa3a2b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> is a periodic function. But then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> is bounded by a constant <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />, i.e. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/b/5ab5a2858299667f808cadac09a84f05c496ecdc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)&lt;M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"78\" height=\"18\" />. Then take, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/0/090b7ae6a0e36353f5f4aa05ee2bfd20f336ee27.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&gt;2M$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"62\" height=\"13\" />. We get that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/6/8e645a0393a2bb5633d525e276321203781753af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,f(b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"49\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/2/7e24db20845eba2e50f55b74a222d4ef4858c53a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(b+f(a)-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"119\" height=\"18\" /> are sides of the triangle, but the first number is greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/6/3266113d5495b881ec783fb0da58a679110d4301.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2M$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> and other two are less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />, which is imposible. We get the contradiction, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/d/9ad99798ec4c38e165cf517cb9e02b1c9e824103.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> could not be greater than 1.\n</p><p>So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/0/d60f9270afb4c3f993c921f9779d6d9a4eb09a56.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u=f(1)=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"101\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Property 1. For any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> \n</p>\n<center> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/7/577d36f19d8078a378cba936d43eb40151b1e13d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(f(x)) = x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"94\" height=\"18\" /> </center>\n<p>Proof. Consider the given condition for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/8/838a259caf8df0b41c91e3aaeff66d6ee9d1c897.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=x$\" width=\"44\" height=\"8\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/5/cf590e9abb33aa9776ddc386b1ba6ee7b43fa413.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"40\" height=\"13\" /> and use Lemma.\n</p><p>Property 2. For any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />\n</p>\n<center> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/8/cd865d6d5edaa36b8e186fa54eb2412a1d9f7170.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x+1)+f(y) &gt; f(x+y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"213\" height=\"18\" />  </center>\n<p>Proof. Consider the given condition for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/5/8758400d80669f83ba8f3c0e7c89caca02288535.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=f(x+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"99\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/0/0a00024b052f63c84ae1882bd40e1a38442bcfae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" /> and use triangle inequality and Property 1.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/1/1e105e34d8e8c53aca79502ddaaecf977c90cf75.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(x)=f(x+1)-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"155\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Property 3. For any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />\n</p>\n<center> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/1/851e339147cbab9b9c06e6686e20fdf50c5040c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(x)+g(y) \\ge g(x+y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"177\" height=\"18\" />  </center>\n<p>Proof. Follows from Property 2.\n</p><p>Property 4. For any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />\n</p>\n<center> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/7/a97d9f69a33c036253e7e9e9df932584c5fb1a30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(nx)+g(my) \\ge g(nx+my)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"235\" height=\"20\" />  </center>\n<p>Proof. Follows from Property 3.\n</p><p>Property 5. For any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, there is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/5/ee5106218fe19fadcc2f2d2251da2ebea0bc8820.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k&gt;n$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"45\" height=\"13\" />, s.t. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/1/a113f38bb785015580d027c25b2131b00e817433.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(k) \\ge k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"70\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>Proof. Because of the Property 1.\n</p><p>Property 6. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/4/7543a500ad662444880b73d431204f4ec1240c26.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(x)=x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"68\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Proof. Suppose, for some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/f/66fe7346c05e5ed807a85747f6c83e2f30012205.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(x)=y\\ne x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"102\" height=\"18\" />. Without lost of generality we can assume that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/4/0b4aee29876af28821f3a35178c09561adaf5a4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x&lt;y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" />. Then there is a number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, such than any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/5/ee5106218fe19fadcc2f2d2251da2ebea0bc8820.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k&gt;n$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"45\" height=\"13\" /> could be represented as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/6/aa6a208b00e405152b364e8a3b379592a4ba9332.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=ax+by$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"96\" height=\"18\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/2/082852571ecc48ed136ba13dcffa8f6e40064bbd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&gt;b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/e/aae7bb3e3dc683ae9c0c28aa1cf9fd25fd07afed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(k)=g(ax+by)\\ge ag(x)+bg(y)=ay+bx&gt;ax+by=k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"475\" height=\"20\" />. That contradicts to the Property 5.\n</p><p>Therefore by definion of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/1/311cabda3a9b09f0dde217303ca9d1cd9201dcf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />,  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/7/4874544e2638f3712dbb70e5ccf37558a5fc0acb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)=x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"69\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_IMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_IMO\" title=\"2009 IMO\">2009 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_IMO_Problems\" title=\"2009 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2009 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2009 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2009 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2009 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2009 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2009 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2009 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017100253\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.029 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.047 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 340/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 894/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 44/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 10625/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    7.030      1 Template:IMO_box\n100.00%    7.030      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:8304:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017100253 and revision id 204542. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}